<p>I downvoted within the first paragraph of the description. Because this follows the escapism that a good number of fictions on this site do: that humans aren’t to blame for all the shitty things we do. Shifting the blame always leaves a bad taste in my mouth. It’s nice to think we’re all cool, but we’re not. Humans are greedy and mean, and I <em>get</em> that it’s fiction, but I can not enjoy something that says otherwise. I’ve simply never bought the “humans are special” mentality.</p>
<p>Anyways, your writing is alright (though I think you should get more familiar with commas) and I see how this sprouted as an idea for clichecon. Your use of the trope is clever and for that I commend you. It’s also a good length for the idea it delivers. I just personally can’t support this.</p>

							</div>

								
					
