														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4120979">
									

<p>Yes, but <em>why</em> are we like that? In this case, <em>SCP-4266 is the reason</em>.</p>
<p>IRL, we simply haven't got a sufficiently large, sufficiently generalised (instead, a mere handful of specially-selected professionals) offworld population yet that any valid comparisons can be drawn between the behaviour of the lucky few who get to call themselves astronauts and the many billions who will spend their entire lives bound to the Earth.</p>
<p>The skip is instead written from a far-future (roughly 23rd century) perspective where tens of thousands (at least) of people from all walks of life left Earth for the colonies in the last 21st, where the expected social problems traceable to humans being inherently nasty markedly failed to manifest.</p>
<p>Sure, the terrestrial human population is demonstrably made up of borderline psychopaths. But what if that was because of a low level Cordyceps type pathogen (which, say, young children tend to take a couple of years to become infected with&#8230;), rather than solely a product of evolution, or worse still &quot;it just is&quot;?</p>
<p>I mean, the entire site is made up of speculative, fantastic fictions. What makes this particular one harder to stomach than, say, a statue made of reinforced concrete that breaks your neck unless you maintain unbroken line of sight on it? That's also clearly not real (&#8230;well, <em>we hope</em>, anyway). It's meant as entertainment, and something that gives you a bit of a spook. The spook here being &quot;something that makes you a little bit crazy, and is an infection that you'd quickly recover from if kept quarantined from it &#8230; but it's in the air worldwide&#8230; there's no escape from it, you're breathing it in continually and being reinfected, with your immune system opting to ignore it because it was an active evolutionary advantage to allow that killer instinct to incorporate itself&quot;&#8230;</p>

							</div>

								
					
