														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4121989">
									

<p>With all due respect, criticizing fiction on the sole basis that you disagree with its message is bad form in a way that I almost find morally unsettling. For instance, a lot of the works on this site are based on the writings of H.P. Lovecraft, who was an outright <em>terrible</em> person who put &quot;messages&quot; in his stories that are far worse than &quot;humans are actually inherently good.&quot; But we still love those stories, not because they say good things (they very clearly don't,) but because they're <em>good as stories.</em></p>
<p>I hope you reconsider your downvote. You admit the article itself is good, clever, and does what it sets out to do - and I agree. Whether or not is clashes with your own personal opinions should be entirely irrelevant.</p>

