			<div class="content" id="post-content-4146695">
									

<p>Lovecraft's thesises and themes are usually fine, especially in his later more mythos-centric work, and still relevant today (maybe more even in a world where it turns out that Bohr was mostly correct, there are enough nuclear weapons to exterminate us a few times, multiple organized genocides have since occured, most of the universe is now known to be invisible, and we might just be in a false vacuum or ancestor simulation anyway). What's problematic about Lovecraft (especially early Lovecraft, but it never goes away entirely) is the casual racism.</p>

